            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(c) When an Employee is required to make extra trips from his or her residence to place of work and return as a result of a Call-In, the Employee shall be paid travel time for reasonable time spent traveling both ways. When the Call-In does not require extra trips, but does involve reporting earlier than the Employee's standard starting time, travel time shall be paid for reasonable time spent traveling from his or her residence to place of work.",
